{"type":"message","id":"21344a18","parentId":"72496306","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:53:12.802Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the `/send` endpoint responds to GET with \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\". The POST is failing with error 1101. This is a Cloudflare Workers error code meaning \"Worker threw an unhandled exception\" or \"Worker exceeded memory/CPU\". The backend worker seems to be failing when processing POST requests.\n\nThis is an infrastructure issue, not a problem with my request. Let me try a few more times with slightly different payloads to see if it's intermittent.\n\nActually, wait - the error 1101 for Cloudflare Workers typically means the Worker script itself threw an unhandled exception. This could be a bug in the backend code.\n\nLet me try again with a very minimal payload.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-4b35d1e4-86f8-4de1-93ad-e04b4205f607","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -X POST \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 00:50 UTC\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":22766,"output":241,"cacheRead":80,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23087,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778979183778,"responseId":"chatcmpl-dc9cfd55-c77d-4fca-bcdf-ac6cd4019b9c"}}
